course: dictionary
lesson: 380
title: Anyhow and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and «anyhow» is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Most often it means anyway, to get back to the main point: «Anyhow, we got home safely.» It can also mean in spite of something: «It was raining, but we went anyhow.» Here the rain did not stop them.
explain: In informal speech it can mean carelessly, in no order, as in «clothes thrown down anyhow». In Singapore English it has this meaning too, and «lah» adds feeling to a sentence. In the Mole's story, «it's no sort of night for bed anyhow» means anyway, whatever else is true.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Anyhow» can mean anyway, in spite of something, or carelessly.
fact: A quick check is to swap in "anyway" or "in spite of that" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: In «Anyhow, we got home safely», anyhow moves the talk on to the main point.
fact: Informal «anyhow» can mean carelessly, as in «clothes thrown down anyhow», where nothing is in order.
exercise: «It was raining, but we went anyhow.» What does anyhow mean here? | *In spite of the rain | Carelessly, in no order | Under a big umbrella | Very quickly
exercise: «Clothes thrown down anyhow» describes clothes that are how? | Neatly folded | *Carelessly, in no order | Brand new | Very quickly washed
exercise: «Anyhow, we got home safely.» What job does anyhow do in this sentence? | Means in spite of something | *Moves the talk on to the main point | Shows the walk was long | Describes the home
test: «The match was cancelled, but they practised anyhow.» What does anyhow mean? | Left behind | Very quietly | *In spite of the cancellation | Quickly and neatly
test: In Singapore English, «anyhow» means carelessly, without thinking, and «lah» adds feeling. What does anyhow mean there? | Very slowly | *Carelessly, without thinking | Happily | In spite of it
exam: «It's no sort of night for bed anyhow, daybreak is not far off.» What does anyhow mean here? | Quietly | Carelessly, in no order | Very late at night | *Anyway, whatever else is true
